  "mainEntity": {
    "name": "Can I Install New Basement Flooring Over a Damp Concrete Slab?",
    "text": "Can I Install New Basement Flooring Over a Damp Concrete Slab?",
    "@type": "Question",
    "answerCount": 1,
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "text": "Question: Can I install new basement flooring over an existing concrete slab that feels slightly cold and damp?\n\nAnswer: You should never install new flooring directly over a concrete slab that feels noticeably damp. Even water-resistant materials like luxury vinyl plank or tile will run into serious trouble if vapor issues are ignored. \n\nTrapping ground moisture beneath an impermeable surface forces water outward toward baseboards, drywall, and framing. Over time, that dampness degrades adhesives, promotes mold behind your trim, and causes floating floor joints to loosen. \n\nThe National Research Council Canada suggests running a 24-hour plastic sheet test: tape a heavy polyethylene sheet tightly to the slab on all four edges. If moisture droplets form underneath or the concrete darkens significantly, moisture is migrating straight through your slab.\n\nWhat to Do Next\nBefore spending money on new materials, take these necessary corrective actions:\n- Inspect exterior downspouts and soil slope to verify surface water is being pushed away from foundation walls.\n- Seal slab cracks with hydraulic compounds or flexible sealants designed for masonry floors.\n- Determine whether a dedicated vapor barrier, dimpled subfloor membrane, or self-leveling underlayment is required by your flooring maker.\n\nWhen moisture testing shows active dampness or your slab is uneven, professional preparation is your safest route. Abraham Becerra and the team at HH Remodeling LLC handle basement remodeling, concrete leveling, and durable flooring installations throughout the Denver metro area. Call 303-505-0866 to get an honest assessment of your basement floor.",
      "@type": "Answer",
      "author": {
        "name": "HH Remodeling LLC",
        "@type": "Organization"
      }
    }
  }
